From e8bff54858cbd22126a044a915d7ef5c95b210a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: joethedev5 <deepsbx1@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 03:43:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 32/41] Reconstruct the process virtual-environment integration

The reference proc carries a virtual_env pointer at offset 1976 in
place of the public subsystem-root path string.  Fork retains it into
the child, exit and forkproc_free release it, and bsd_init clears it.

kern_exec now creates the environment from a posix_spawn subsystem
root, installs one supplied by a new PSPA_VIRTUAL_ENV port action
(with the com.apple.private.virtualenv.spawn entitlement and the
single-environment restriction), publishes its path to image_params,
and releases the port in exec_port_actions_destroy.

Authored-By: joethedev5 <joeshmo@nunya.com>
---
